OL,3,GNEWSALong-delayed CalMac ferry Glen
OL,4,ARosa begins sea trials
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe second of two long-delayed ferries
OL,7,Fbuilt at the Ferguson Marine shipyard
OL,8,Fhas set off for its builder's sea
OL,9,Ftrials.
OL,11,FThe 335ft (102m) long Glen Rosa set
OL,12,Fsail from Inchgreen quayside in
OL,13,FGreenock earlier, its first journey
OL,14,Funder its own power.
OL,16,FIt will undergo tests in the Firth of
OL,17,FClyde, with specialists checking its
OL,18,Fhandling and propulsion systems.
OL,20,FGlen Rosa's sister vessel, MV Glen
OL,21,FSannox, entered service with CalMac in
OL,22,FJanuary 2025 after years of delays.
OL,23,APub: 12-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
